{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_background_argument_skeleton", "label": "Chapter 2 Argument Skeleton (B1-B16)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exists because the 63 extracted verdicts hold none of the chapter's arguments; composing from the verdicts alone would rebuild the citations and lose the reasoning, and the reasoning is what discharges D7."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b1_globality_estimation_budget", "label": "B1 \u2014 Globality Is an Estimation-Budget Argument", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reading globality as a similarity assumption is rejected because the source explicitly disclaims it; small-collection pooling is therefore an extension by analogy stated as a falsifiable conjecture."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b2_weather_adjudication", "label": "B2 \u2014 The Energy-versus-Hospitality Weather Adjudication", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Electrical load couples to weather physically; bar revenue couples only through a person's decision to go out, so nothing licenses carrying an effect size across that gap. Position reached: weather must earn its place, not that it will not help."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b3_median_versus_mean", "label": "B3 \u2014 The Median-versus-Mean Functional Argument", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A cost objective in place of an error measure is rejected because its parameters are undefined for a quantity that is not a replenishment quantity \u2014 a property of the problem, not a convenience."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b4_false_alarm_asymmetry", "label": "B4 \u2014 The False-Alarm Asymmetry at Graded Evidential Strength", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dixon is a 32-participant laboratory study reported as a direction without an effect size, so the asymmetry is asserted at that strength and no higher; Ancker's magnitudes do not transfer, the mechanism does."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b5_structural_closure", "label": "B5 \u2014 Structural Closure, Not Sparsity, Breaks the Distinct-Scores Condition", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b6_recorded_regime_extension", "label": "B6 \u2014 The Recorded-Regime Extension of CPTC", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If misclassification is the currency the bound is paid in, a regime variable that is simply recorded costs nothing \u2014 valid a fortiori, and stated with its limit that no guarantee about an online procedure carries across to a static band."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b7_kostenko_correction", "label": "B7 \u2014 Kostenko's Correction Moves the Label, Not the Estimator Choice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b10_vendor_instability", "label": "B10 \u2014 A Vendor Report Volunteering Its Own Instability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sharper evidence for rank instability than either dedicated source supplies, because it arrives from a party with an interest in the ordering being stable."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_b14_prism_gap_construction", "label": "B14 \u2014 The Construction of the Gap from PRISM", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_owned_derivation", "label": "The OWNED Marking for Derivations the Chapter Reasons Itself", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Marks the rows where the chapter reasons past its sources; those are the rows a careless compression turns back into knowledge-telling, and the rows attribution defects were previously found in."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_background_argument_skeleton_boundary_check_three_answers", "label": "The Chapter 2 / Chapter 3 Boundary Check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/background_argument_skeleton.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Framing it as Methods-can-carry or Methods-cannot is the trap, because it treats relocation as the assumed outcome; the third answer is that Me